#
# nwell_isolation.drc -- the n-well rules `klt drc --deck sky130` does not
# carry, transcribed verbatim from the sky130A PDK's own KLayout deck
# (issue #122).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# This sub-block's whole subject is a deliberate n-well SPLIT: three
# electrically distinct well islands, one per PFET body domain, where a
# conventional layout would have drawn a single VDD-tied well (see
# ../bin/build_layout.py's "THE RECIPE" docstring and
# design/sampling_frontend.sch's DR-004 body-tie requirement).
#
# `klt drc --deck sky130`'s curated rule table (klt 0.3.0) contains **no
# n-well rules at all** -- no width, no spacing, no enclosure. Its rule ids
# cover poly/diff/li1/mcon/met1..met5/via..via4/capm/capm2 and nothing on
# layer 64 (nwell). So a split-well layout passes that deck *vacuously on
# exactly the rules that govern the split*: draw the two islands 0.5 um
# apart -- illegal, and physically one merged well on silicon -- and `klt
# drc --deck sky130` still reports "clean". Verified directly (two 2x2 um
# nwell rectangles 0.5 um apart: `status: clean, violation_count: 0`).
#
# `klt drc --engine klayout --pdk sky130A` does not close the gap either: it
# resolves the PDK's own `sky130A.lydrc`, but that deck defaults its
# front-end-of-line rule group off (`FEOL = false` at the top of the file)
# and klt's klayout engine at the 0.3.0 pin passes only `-rd input=` /
# `-rd report=`, with no way to set the deck variables that would switch
# FEOL on. The same 0.5 um fixture comes back "clean" through that path too
# -- and, because the klayout engine reports an empty `coverage` block,
# nothing in the envelope says an entire rule group was skipped.
#
# Both findings are filed generically, with no design content, at
# 2AMLogic/klayout-tools per CLAUDE.md's friction protocol:
#
#   - the missing well-layer rules in the curated deck:
#     2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1420 (filed by this issue);
#   - the deck-variable gap in the klayout engine:
#     2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1302, already filed and CLOSED upstream on
#     2026-08-22 -- but 0.3.0 is still the newest release on PyPI as of
#     2026-08-25, so the fix is not in this repo's pin yet. When a release
#     carrying it lands and layout/requirements.txt moves to it, re-check
#     whether the PDK's own FEOL group can be driven directly; if it can,
#     retire this deck rather than maintaining a transcription in parallel.
#
# So this deck carries the three rules the isolation claim actually rests
# on, and `../bin/run-flow.sh` runs it through `klt drc --engine klayout
# --deck-file` (klt is still the runner and the report parser) plus a
# negative-control fixture (`nwell_isolation_fixture.json`) that proves it
# fires. A "clean" verdict here means something only because the fixture
# shows "violations" is reachable on the same deck in the same run.
#
# PROVENANCE (transcribed, not invented)
# --------------------------------------
# Every threshold below is copied from
# `$PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/klayout/drc/sky130A.lydrc` at the open_pdks
# commit sim/pdk.json pins (c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b):
#
#   line 212  nwell.width(0.84, euclidian)        -> "nwell.1"
#   line 213  nwell.isolated(1.27, euclidian)     -> "nwell.2a"
#   line 276  nwell.enclosing(tap.not(uhvi).and(nsdm), 0.18, euclidian)
#                                                 -> "difftap.10"
#
# ONE APPROXIMATION, stated rather than hidden: the official `difftap.10`
# scopes its tap to `nsdm` (the n+ implant marker). No generator or drawn
# shape in this repo's layout flow emits implant layers at all -- `klt gen`
# draws nwell/diff/poly/licon1/li1 only, and ../bin/build_layout.py adds
# tap/licon1/li1/mcon/met1/via/met2 -- so `nsdm` is absent from the stream
# and the official rule would match nothing. Every `tap` (65/44) shape in
# this layout is an n+ well tie inside an n-well by construction, so
# dropping the `and(nsdm)` term is exact *for this layout* while being a
# widening of the rule in general. `difftap.8` (p+diff enclosure by nwell,
# 0.18 um) is scoped the same way, to `diff` that interacts with `nwell` --
# in this PFET-only cell that is precisely the p+ diffusion.
#
# Rules deliberately NOT transcribed: everything outside the well/tap
# family. This is not a general-purpose FEOL deck and must not be read as
# one -- `klt drc --deck sky130` remains the authority for the rules it does
# carry, and `../README.md` states plainly which rule families neither deck
# checks.
#
# Usage (klt is the runner; this file is only the rule text):
#
#   klt drc <layout.gds> --engine klayout \
#       --deck-file layout/sampling-frontend-wells/drc/nwell_isolation.drc \
#       --format json
#

if $input
  source($input)
end

if $report
  report("sky130 n-well isolation rules (sky130-sar-adc #122)", $report)
else
  report("sky130 n-well isolation rules (sky130-sar-adc #122)", "nwell_isolation.lyrdb")
end

# Hierarchical mode, matching the PDK deck's own setting.
deep

nwell = input(64, 20)
diff  = input(65, 20)
tap   = input(65, 44)

# nwell.1 : min. nwell width : 0.84um  (sky130A.lydrc line 212)
nwell.width(0.84, euclidian).output(
  "nwell.1", "nwell.1 : min. nwell width : 0.84um")

# nwell.2a : min. nwell spacing (merged if less) : 1.27um
# (sky130A.lydrc line 213).  THE rule this sub-block's well split rests on:
# two islands closer than this are not separate wells at all.
nwell.isolated(1.27, euclidian).output(
  "nwell.2a", "nwell.2a : min. nwell spacing (merged if less) : 1.27um")

# difftap.8 : min. p+diff enclosure by nwell : 0.18um (sky130A.lydrc line
# 274), scoped to diff interacting with nwell in place of the official
# `and(psdm)` -- see the approximation note in this file's header.
nwell.enclosing(diff.interacting(nwell), 0.18, euclidian).output(
  "difftap.8", "difftap.8 : min. p+diff enclosure by nwell : 0.18um")

# difftap.10 : min. n+tap enclosure by nwell : 0.18um (sky130A.lydrc line
# 276), scoped to every drawn tap in place of the official `and(nsdm)` --
# see the approximation note in this file's header.
nwell.enclosing(tap, 0.18, euclidian).output(
  "difftap.10", "difftap.10 : min. n+tap enclosure by nwell : 0.18um")
